  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Deflazacort may be considered for the treatment of Becker Muscular Dystrophy, based on its association with Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy, which in turn is linked to two other therapies—Golodirsen and Eteplirsen—both of which are indicated for Becker Muscular Dystrophy. These pathways indicate a potential mechanism of action where Deflazacort could be part of a therapeutic strategy targeting the underlying pathology of Becker Muscular Dystrophy. The high scores across the three paths suggest a consistent level of confidence in the relationship, though the specific mechanisms by which Deflazacort exerts its effects remain unclear. The evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, but further research is needed to determine the exact role of Deflazacort in this context.",
